Last Updated: July 23, 2026

This Atum Labs, Inc. Examples Repository Proprietary Reference Implementation License Agreement ("Agreement") governs access to and use of the private GitHub repository currently located at github.com/Atum-Labs/examples, together with all current and future source code, sample applications, reference implementations, snippets, scripts, configuration files, environment templates, tests, CI/CD workflows, documentation, diagrams, data, and other materials included in that repository (collectively, the "Repository Materials"), except for any material that expressly states that it is governed by a different license.

This Agreement is a proprietary license and is not an open source license.

By accessing, cloning, downloading, copying, viewing, running, modifying, contributing to, or otherwise using any Repository Materials, you agree to this Agreement both individually and, if applicable, on behalf of the company or other legal entity for which you act (the "Licensee"). You represent that you have authority to bind Licensee. If you do not agree or lack that authority, do not access or use the Repository Materials.

1. PURPOSE AND STATUS OF THE REPOSITORY

1.1 Authorized Purpose. Atum makes the Repository Materials available solely to enable Licensee to:

(a) evaluate and understand Atum-authorized products, services, APIs, software development kits, packages, payment flows, and integration patterns;

(b) study, copy, run, test, adapt, and modify the Repository Materials to design and develop Licensee's own software applications that interoperate with Atum-authorized products or services (each, a "Licensee Application");

(c) test, demonstrate, validate, deploy, maintain, and operate a Licensee Application, including in production, subject to any separate rights required to access or use applicable Atum packages, APIs, services, networks, contracts, or other resources; and

(d) conduct an Atum-authorized pilot, proof of concept, security review, operational-readiness review, or integration assessment relating to a Licensee Application.

The activities in Sections 1.1(a) through 1.1(d) are the "Authorized Purpose." No other purpose is permitted.

1.2 Reference implementations only. The Repository Materials are examples and reference implementations intended to assist developers in building their own applications. They are not, merely by being included in the Repository, a production release, supported product, authoritative specification, certification, or promise of continued availability, compatibility, maintenance, monitoring, or support.

1.3 Supported configurations. Licensee may use the Repository Materials only with the packages, versions, endpoints, services, chains, assets, corridors, contracts, credentials, and configurations that Atum then designates for the applicable use. The presence of any package reference, endpoint, service, chain, asset, corridor, contract, configuration, or code path in the Repository does not by itself mean that it is available, authorized, current, or supported. Repository documentation may impose narrower technical or operational conditions but does not expand the rights granted by this Agreement.

1.4 Expanding library. Unless a file or directory expressly states otherwise, this Agreement applies to all examples and other Repository Materials later added to the Repository, as well as the Repository Materials present on the Last Updated date above.

2. LICENSE GRANT

2.1 Repository license. Subject to Licensee's continuing compliance with this Agreement and Atum's continuing authorization of Licensee's repository access, Atum grants Licensee, during the period in which such access remains authorized, a limited, revocable, non-exclusive, non-transferable, non-sublicensable license to:

(a) permit Licensee personnel and individual contractors who have a legitimate need to know, are authorized by Atum to access the Repository, and are bound by written obligations at least as protective as this Agreement ("Authorized Users") to access and clone the Repository into Licensee-controlled, secure systems;

(b) internally view, copy, run, test, evaluate, adapt, and modify the Repository Materials solely for the Authorized Purpose;

(c) create modifications and derivative works of the Repository Materials solely as reasonably necessary to design, build, test, validate, deploy, maintain, and operate a Licensee Application;

(d) incorporate portions of the Repository Materials into a Licensee Application solely to the extent reasonably necessary for the Licensee Application to interoperate with Atum-authorized products or services;

(e) deploy and operate a Licensee Application, including in production, solely for the Authorized Purpose; and

(f) make a reasonable number of secure backup copies solely for disaster recovery and continuity of the Authorized Purpose.

2.2 No distribution of reference library. Licensee may distribute or make a Licensee Application available to its own users or customers only in compiled, hosted, or otherwise non-source form that does not expose, disclose, or permit extraction or separate reuse of the Repository Materials. No right is granted to distribute the Repository Materials in source form, publish them as examples or templates, provide them as a standalone library or implementation kit, or allow any third party to extract, reuse, or separately exploit them.

2.3 Continuing application rights after access ends. If Atum suspends, revokes, or otherwise ends Licensee's Repository access for convenience and not because of Licensee's breach, Licensee may continue to operate and maintain a Licensee Application developed in compliance with this Agreement before access ended, provided that Licensee:

(a) ceases all further Repository access and all new development using standalone copies of the Repository Materials;

(b) does not expose, disclose, distribute, or permit extraction or separate reuse of the Repository Materials;

(c) continues to comply with Sections 4 through 12, 14, 16, and 17 and all other provisions that by their nature continue to apply;

(d) maintains any separate authorization required to use applicable Atum packages, APIs, services, networks, contracts, or other resources; and

(e) does not use retained Repository Materials to build new applications, new integrations, or material new functionality after Repository access ends.

For clarity, ending Repository access does not itself terminate any separately granted right to use an Atum package, API, service, network, or other resource, and termination of such a separate right does not itself require Licensee to discontinue portions of a Licensee Application that do not depend on that resource.

2.4 No implied rights. No other rights are granted, whether by implication, estoppel, exhaustion, or otherwise.

