13. TERM, ACCESS REVOCATION, SUSPENSION, AND TERMINATION

13.1 Subject to Section 16.1, this Agreement begins when Licensee first accesses the Repository Materials (the "Effective Date") and continues until terminated (the "Term").

13.2 Discretionary access. Atum may suspend or revoke Licensee's access to the Repository at any time, with or without cause or advance notice. Repository access is discretionary and does not create any entitlement to continued access, updates, maintenance, support, or future examples.

13.3 Suspension for risk. Atum may suspend access to the Repository or require Licensee to stop using affected Repository Materials immediately if Atum reasonably believes there is a breach, security risk, unauthorized use, legal risk, threat to Atum systems or users, or other material risk.

13.4 Termination. Except to the extent an applicable Customer Agreement provides otherwise, either party may terminate this Agreement for convenience on ten days' written notice. Atum may terminate immediately upon: (a) breach of Sections 2 through 10; (b) unauthorized disclosure, public posting, competitive misuse, or unauthorized security testing; (c) infringement or misappropriation of Atum intellectual property; (d) Licensee no longer being an authorized Atum customer, partner, pilot participant, or collaborator; or (e) termination or expiration of the relationship or separate agreement that supported Licensee's access.

13.5 Effect of convenience revocation or termination. If Repository access is revoked or this Agreement is terminated for convenience and not because of Licensee's breach:

(a) Licensee must immediately cease accessing the Repository and cease using standalone copies of the Repository Materials for new development;

(b) Licensee must delete standalone clones, forks, archives, and copies of the Repository Materials that are not reasonably necessary to operate or maintain a Licensee Application developed before access ended;

(c) Repository Materials retained within or reasonably necessary to operate or maintain such a Licensee Application remain subject to this Agreement and may not be separately accessed, extracted, reused, disclosed, sublicensed, or distributed;

(d) Licensee may continue operating and maintaining that Licensee Application only in accordance with Section 2.3; and

(e) upon Atum's reasonable request, Licensee must certify compliance with this Section.

13.6 Effect of termination for breach or risk. If Atum terminates this Agreement or revokes access because of Licensee's breach, unauthorized disclosure, competitive misuse, security threat, infringement, misappropriation, or unlawful conduct, Atum may require Licensee to:

(a) immediately cease all access to and use of the Repository Materials;

(b) stop operating, distributing, or making available any Licensee Application to the extent it contains, exposes, depends upon, or was developed through material misuse of the Repository Materials;

(c) remove the Repository Materials and all modifications and derivative works of them from active systems, deployments, CI/CD systems, developer devices, and shared storage;

(d) destroy all copies, clones, forks, archives, caches, backups, build artifacts, container images, compiled forms, and derivatives containing Repository Materials, except for one inaccessible archival copy retained solely if required by law; and

(e) certify destruction and cessation in writing upon Atum's request.

13.7 Separate Atum resources. Suspension, revocation, or termination of Repository access does not prevent Atum from separately suspending, revoking, or terminating Licensee's access to any Atum package, API, service, network, contract, credential, or other resource in accordance with the terms governing that resource.

13.8 Survival. Termination does not affect rights or obligations accrued before termination. Sections 2.2 through 2.4, 4 through 12, 13.5 through 13.8, 14, 16, 17, and any provisions that by their nature should survive will survive termination.

